# Used only for offline sandbox evaluation. Never use real application data.
# Default Compose needs no auth configuration; protected APIs return 503.
# Only the optional compose.auth.yaml overlay requires this readable file.
# Leave unset by default. For the optional overlay only, set this in the
# environment or uncomment it in an explicitly selected --env-file.
# SANDBOX_AUTH_CONFIG_FILE=/operator/supplied/sandbox-auth.json
# Validate default configuration: docker compose config --quiet
# Validate opt-in configuration after supplying the file path:
# docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.auth.yaml config --quiet
# JSON array, strictly these keys; subject must match sandbox-[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]{0,55}.
# Each entry: tokenSha256 = 64 lowercase hex SHA256 digest, subject, scopes.
# scopes is a nonempty unique subset of profile:read and profile:write.
# Provision a random base64url bearer (32-256 characters) separately and keep it secret.
# Store only its SHA256 digest in the config, never the clear bearer.
# No token issuance, user identity, production auth, app sync, or real data support.
